<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luís António de Sousa Botelho Mourão</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1722–1798</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luís António de Sousa Botelho Mourão, known by his title as the Morgado de Mateus, was a Portuguese nobleman who governed the restored Captaincy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-paulo">São Paulo</a> from 1765 to 1775. Sent under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marquis-of-pombal">Marquis of Pombal</a>, he rebuilt the captaincy's administration and militia, promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> cultivation and founded new settlements and forts on the frontier with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-america">Spanish America</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luis-antonio-de-sousa-botelho-mourao.jpg" alt="Luís António de Sousa Botelho Mourão" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:D._Lu%C3%ADs_Ant%C3%B3nio_de_Sousa_Botelho_Mour%C3%A3o,_4.%C2%BA_Morgado_de_Mateus.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
